SELECT 'OPS-LOG-OWNER-SESSION-1: qnfo-ops redactSecrets does not mask the owner session token (qos_ + 64 hex), so owner_verify results reach ops_ai_log and ops_jobs in clear',
 'Charter pillar: security. Doer: qnfo-ops via qnfo-code-orchestrator. Measured 2026-11-05: 22 ops_ai_log rows and 4 ops_jobs rows since 2026-09-01 held a live-format owner session token (qos_ + 64 hex, valid 12 hours) in tool_calls/response/payload; migrations/2026-11-05-c2-ops-log-owner-session-scrub.sql removed the stored values. Cause: redactSecrets (qnfo-ops/worker.js) rule 1783 needs a word boundary and the underscore of qos_ is a word character, rule 1784 needs an upper-case letter and the token is lower-case hex, and the key rule at 1769 lists token/secret/password names but not owner_session. Lever: add a rule that masks qos_ followed by 16 or more hex characters wherever it appears, and add owner_session to the key list; add cases to qnfo-ops/log-redact.test.mjs (a bare token, a JSON-escaped token inside a tool_calls summary, a token that follows owner_session). Done: log-redact.test.mjs passes with the new cases, qnfo-ops is deployed with the version above this issue, and after the next owner login the newest ops_ai_log tool_calls row for owner_verify holds no qos_ followed by 64 hex characters.
